## Context
Nomination from the sen-causal-reading session (2026-10-15). `/healthcheck`
is long to type and is the only non-draconic name among the session-hygiene
skills (lair, molt, perch, roar). Proposed: `yawn`, four letters, the dragon
waking and stretching before work. No existing use of `yawn` in the harness.

Author decision (2026-10-15): use `yawn`, without a transition alias or legacy
compatibility entry point. Migrate live callers and installed registrations.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Skill renamed `yawn`; every reference updated in one commit (15 files
      in skills, rules, tests, Makefile, scripts, hooks; molt calls it).
- [ ] No `/healthcheck` alias or legacy compatibility entry point remains;
      live callers and installed registrations use `yawn`.
- [ ] `make skills-catalog` regenerated; `make check-skills-drift` and
      `make check` pass.

## Raid Imagine — 2026-10-15
Imagine: author approved one atomic PR exceeding 15 files on 2026-10-15. Update live identifiers/callers/registrations; historical evidence retains former names. Installer discovers canonical skills dynamically; validate managed projections after canonical merge.

## Raid Plan — 2026-10-15
Actions: adapt real installer discovery/idempotence test to yawn first, then atomic move/frontmatter/live callers/support inventory/test identifiers and catalog. Preserve historical records. Post-merge migrate managed registrations from active primary checkout and read back. Gates: focused adapter/projection/seam/molt/session-scratch/project-state tests, skills-catalog, drift, full make check. Author authorized >15-path atomic exception. Shared paths with 1105: README, lair, roar; execute/verify sequentially.
